# 📖 Bible Full-Text Search (FTS)

This project demonstrates how to build a **.NET 8 Web API** that integrates with **Elasticsearch** and **Kibana** to perform full-text search (FTS) over the entire Bible text.  
The dataset used comes from [Biblia Livre](https://github.com/blivre/BibliaLivre), in the “verse-per-line” format (`bliv-n4_vpl.zip`).

---

## 🧩 Tech Stack

| Component | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| **.NET 8 (C#)** | API and business logic |
| **Elasticsearch** | Full-text search engine |
| **Kibana** | Visualization and query interface for Elasticsearch |
| **Docker & Docker Compose** | Environment orchestration |
| **Swagger / OpenAPI** | API documentation and testing UI |

---

## ⚙️ Project Structure

```
bible-fts/
├─ BibleFTS.Api/ # .NET Web API
├─ BibleFTS.Tests/ # .NET Web API Tests
├─ data/
│ └─ bliv-n4_vpl.zip # Bible dataset (verse-per-line format)
├─ bible-fts.sln
├─ docker-compose.yml
├─ LICENSE
├─ README.md
└─ ...
```

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Prerequisites

Make sure the following are installed:

- **Docker** & **Docker Compose**
- **Git**

> ⚠️ .NET SDK is optional — you only need it for local development outside Docker.

---

### 2. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Murilo-Rainho/bible-fts.git
cd bible-fts
```

### 3. Ensure the Dataset is ok
Ensure the dataset is here:
```
bible-fts/
 ├─ data/
 │   └─ bliv-n4_vpl.zip
```
If there was nothing, download the bliv-n4_vpl.zip [here](https://github.com/blivre/BibliaLivre/releases).

### 4. Build and Run with Docker
From the project root:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

### 5 Check if application is running
This will start:

>API (Swagger) → http://localhost:8080/swagger/index.html
>
>Elasticsearch → http://localhost:9200
>
>Kibana → http://localhost:5601/app/home#/

You can check container status anytime with:

```bash
docker compose ps
```

API Endpoints
After the containers are up, open [Swagger UI](http://localhost:8080/swagger/index.html)

#### Available Routes
|     Method    |              Endpoint              |               Description              |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
|     POST      |           /api/bible/seed          |  Elasticsearch with the Bible dataset  |
|      GET      |  /api/bible/search?query=anything  |       Performs a full-text search      |
|     DELETE    |           /api/bible/all           |       Deletes all indexed verses       |
|      GET      |       /api/bible/health/index      |       Checks if the index exists       |

### 6 Seed database
Wtih all application running perfectly, just seed ES

```http
Run POST /api/bible/seed
```

## 💡 Development Tips
- To rebuild from scratch (remove all data & containers):

```bash
docker compose down -v
docker compose up --build
```

[Open Swagger](http://localhost:8080/swagger/index.html) and

```http
Run POST /api/bible/seed
```

- To check containers logs:

```bash
docker compose logs -f api
```

- Explore data in Kibana

Kibana → Dev Tools → Console (with "bible" index)

Example:
```kibana
GET bible/_search
{
  "query": {
    "match_phrase": {
      "text": "ido com Davi"
    }
  }
}
```

## ✍️ Example Workflow
Start the stack:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

[Open Swagger](http://localhost:8080/swagger/index.html)

```http
Run POST /api/bible/seed
```

Wait until seeding finishes (it may take a few seconds)

Run a search:

```http
GET /api/bible/search?query=Deus%20criou
```

[Open Kibana](http://localhost:5601/app/home#/) → Dev Tools → Console (with "bible" index)

Example:
```kibana
GET bible/_search
{
  "query": {
    "match_phrase": {
      "text": "Deus criou"
    }
  }
}
```

#### Environment Variables
|       Variable      |           Default           |        Description       |
| ------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------ |
|  ELASTICSEARCH_URL  |	 http://elasticsearch:9200  |  Elasticsearch endpoint  |
|   ASPNETCORE_URLS   |        http://+:8080        |     API listening URL    |

